        "text": "**Trace of `POST /projects/{project_id}/ask`**\n\n1. **Retrieval selection** (`create_app.ask`, S4): the handler calls `runtime.retrieval(project_id, runtime.embedding_config(body.embedding), compatible=body.method != \"lexical\")`, so a \"lexical\" request sets `compatible=False`. It then builds `GroundedQAService(retrieval, RAGContextBuilder(), QAPromptBuilder(), create_llm(runtime, body.llm))` and calls `service.answer(QARequest(question=body.question, project_id=project_id, retrieval_method=body.method, max_tokens=body.max_tokens))`.\n\n2. **Answer generation** (`GroundedQAService.answer`, S3): the service validates the request, then runs `_retrieve(request)`, `_focus_on_named_symbol(...)`, `_context(..., request.max_context_chars)`, and `_citations(context)`. If `context.blocks` is empty, it returns a `QAAnswer` with `NO_EVIDENCE_ANSWER`, empty citations, and `llm_model/llm_provider/finish_reason=None` — no LLM call. Otherwise it builds prompts via `self.prompt_builder.build(request.question, context)` and calls `self.llm_provider.generate(LLMRequest(prompt, system_prompt, temperature, max_tokens))`. An `LLMProviderError` is re-raised as `QAError(\"llm\", ...)`. The returned `QAAnswer` carries `response.text`, `citations`, `retrieval_method`, `omitted_context_count`, `llm_model`, `llm_provider`, and `finish_reason`.\n\n3. **Trusted citation hydration** (S4 + `APIRuntime.citation_chunks`, S2): the endpoint collects chunk IDs from `answer.citations` and calls `runtime.citation_chunks(project_id, ...)`, which dedupes IDs, fetches rows via `store.get_chunks_by_chunk_ids`, and validates that every requested chunk exists and each chunk's `file_id` maps to a source file whose `relative_path` matches the chunk's. Any mismatch raises `APIError(500, \"citation_metadata_missing\", ...)`. Valid chunks feed `AskResponse` citations via `_citation(chunks[item.chunk_id])`.\n\nThe test (S1) confirms the hydrated citation's `file_id`/`symbol_id`/`source_file` match the stored chunk and `llm.calls == 1`.",
